## Summary Report: MonoDreams Web Browser (WASM) Bootstrap Analysis

Based on a thorough exploration of the MonoDreams codebase, here is a detailed map of how the games bootstrap and run, organized by your four research areas:

---

### 1. APPLICATION ENTRY POINTS

**MonoDreams.Examples**
- **File:** `/Users/rodrigooliveira/git/roo-oliv/monodreams/.worktrees/feat/kni/MonoDreams.Examples/Program.cs`
- **Code:**
  ```csharp
  using var game = new Game1(args);
  game.Run();
  ```

**MonoDreams.Demos**
- **File:** `/Users/rodrigooliveira/git/roo-oliv/monodreams/.worktrees/feat/kni/MonoDreams.Demos/Program.cs`
- **Code:**
  ```csharp
  using var game = new Game1(args);
  game.Run();
  ```

Both projects instantiate and immediately call `.Run()` on their respective `Game1` classes, which inherit from MonoGame's `Game` base class. The `Game.Run()` method enters the platform-specific event loop.

**Game1 Classes:**
- **Examples Game1:** `/Users/rodrigooliveira/git/roo-oliv/monodreams/.worktrees/feat/kni/MonoDreams.Examples/Game1.cs` (199 lines)
- **Demos Game1:** `/Users/rodrigooliveira/git/roo-oliv/monodreams/.worktrees/feat/kni/MonoDreams.Demos/Game1.cs` (180 lines)

Both accept `string[] args` in the constructor and check for `--headless` flag for testing scenarios.

---

### 2. MAIN `Game` SUBCLASSES: LIFECYCLE & CONFIGURATION

#### **Game1 (Examples) — Class Definition**
**File:** `/Users/rodrigooliveira/git/roo-oliv/monodreams/.worktrees/feat/kni/MonoDreams.Examples/Game1.cs`

**Constructor (lines 35–70):**
```csharp
public Game1(string[] args = null)
{
    _headless = args?.Contains("--headless") ?? false;
    _settings = SettingsManager.Instance.Settings;

    _graphics = new GraphicsDeviceManager(this);
    Content.RootDirectory = "Content";
    IsMouseVisible = false;
    _graphics.GraphicsProfile = GraphicsProfile.HiDef;

    if (_headless)
    {
        _graphics.PreferredBackBufferWidth = 1;
        _graphics.PreferredBackBufferHeight = 1;
        _graphics.SynchronizeWithVerticalRetrace = false;
        IsFixedTimeStep = false;
    }
    else
    {
        IsFixedTimeStep = true;
        _graphics.IsFullScreen = _settings.IsFullscreen;
        _graphics.PreferredBackBufferWidth = _settings.WindowWidth;
        _graphics.PreferredBackBufferHeight = _settings.WindowHeight;
        _graphics.SynchronizeWithVerticalRetrace = true;
    }
    _graphics.ApplyChanges();

    _viewportManager = new(this, _settings.VirtualWidth, _settings.VirtualHeight);
    _camera = new(_settings.VirtualWidth, _settings.VirtualHeight);
    Window.ClientSizeChanged += OnWindowResize;
}
```

**GraphicsDeviceManager Configuration:**
- **Profile:** `GraphicsProfile.HiDef` (always)
- **VSync:** `true` in normal mode, `false` in headless
- **Fixed Timestep:** `true` in normal mode, `false` in headless
- **Backbuffer:** From settings (1920x1080 defaults) in normal mode; 1x1 in headless mode
- **Fullscreen:** Controlled via `GameSettings.IsFullscreen` (default: false)

**Headless Mode Details:**
- Renders to a 1x1 window positioned off-screen at (-2000, -2000) (line 92)
- Skips drawing entirely: `if (_headless) return;` in `Draw()` (line 165)
- Runs at max speed (no VSync, no fixed timestep)
- Used for logic/replay testing only

**Window/Resolution Setup:**
- **Virtual Resolution:** Loaded from `GameSettings` (1920x1080 default)
- **Actual Backbuffer:** Also from `GameSettings` (1920x1080 default)
- **Viewport Scaling:** Handled by `ViewportManager` with three modes: PixelPerfect, Smooth, KeepAspectRatio (line 99–104)
- **Window Resize Handling:** `Window.ClientSizeChanged` event (line 69) calls `InitializeRenderer()` to recalculate viewport

**Lifecycle Overrides:**

| Method | Purpose | Lines |
|--------|---------|-------|
| `Initialize()` | Logger init, SettingsManager, screen registration, input replay plan loading | 84–148 |
| `Update(GameTime)` | Input polling, screen controller update | 150–161 |
| `Draw(GameTime)` | Skipped in headless; otherwise delegates to screen controller | 163–173 |
| `Dispose(bool)` | Logger shutdown, runner cleanup, resource disposal | 187–198 |

---

#### **Game1 (Demos) — Class Definition**
**File:** `/Users/rodrigooliveira/git/roo-oliv/monodreams/.worktrees/feat/kni/MonoDreams.Demos/Game1.cs`

**Constructor (lines 32–63):**
```csharp
public Game1(string[]? args = null)
{
    _headless = HeadlessOptions.Parse(args);

    _graphics = new GraphicsDeviceManager(this);
    Content.RootDirectory = "Content";
    IsMouseVisible = false;
    _graphics.GraphicsProfile = GraphicsProfile.HiDef;

    _graphics.PreferredBackBufferWidth = VirtualWidth;  // 1280
    _graphics.PreferredBackBufferHeight = VirtualHeight; // 720
    if (_headless.Enabled)
    {
        _graphics.SynchronizeWithVerticalRetrace = false;
        IsFixedTimeStep = false;
    }
    else
    {
        _graphics.SynchronizeWithVerticalRetrace = true;
        IsFixedTimeStep = true;
    }
    _graphics.ApplyChanges();

    _viewportManager = new ViewportManager(this, VirtualWidth, VirtualHeight);
    _camera = new Camera(VirtualWidth, VirtualHeight);
    Window.ClientSizeChanged += (_, _) => InitializeRenderer(...);
}
```

**Key Difference from Examples:** Demos uses hardcoded virtual resolution (1280x720 constants on lines 18–19) rather than loading from settings.

**Headless Mode (Demos):**
- **Enabled by:** `HeadlessOptions.Parse(args)` (parses `--headless`, `--screen`, `--frames`, `--capture-every`, `--sample-every` flags)
- **Full Rendering:** Unlike Examples, Demos **does NOT skip drawing** in headless mode (line 128 comment: "rendering every frame is what makes screenshots and render-path memory behaviour observable")
- **Window Position:** Off-screen at (-2000, -2000) (line 85)
- **Screenshot Capture:** Enabled via `ScreenshotCaptureSystem` (line 86)
- **Auto-exit:** After N frames (line 163–167)
- **Heap Sampling:** Periodic GC.GetTotalMemory() samples logged (line 153)

**Lifecycle:**

| Method | Purpose | Lines |
|--------|---------|-------|
| `Initialize()` | Logger init, screen registration, optional screenshot capture setup | 72–115 |
| `Update(GameTime)` | Input polling (Q to exit), screen update | 117–124 |
| `Draw(GameTime)` | Always renders (headless or not); calls `DriveHeadless()` if headless | 126–135 |
| `DriveHeadless(GameTime)` | Heap sampling, screenshot capture, frame counting, auto-exit | 140–168 |

